! lararium-browser Deletion Map

Inventory of every sovereignty shore, web2 smell, and page-singleton residue
touching the browser vessel surface. Four classifications:

| Class | Meaning |
|---|---|
| ''Constitutional'' | Belongs in the browser vessel as-is. Satisfies BV-1–BV-7. |
| ''Adapter'' | DOM or page-global dependency that stays, behind one named adapter boundary. Never crosses worker-side. |
| ''Quarantine'' | Carries a mix of constitutional and residue; the residue stays behind the adapter boundary. |
| ''Dead residue'' | Whole-page singleton or web2 smell. Stays out of the package. |

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shore-inventory`>>

!! Shore Inventory

!!! packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-browser-surface.ts

| Shore | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `mountPanel(engine, container: HTMLElement)` | Adapter | The host calls it; the body couples `window.document`, `shadowRoot`, and `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate`. It stands as the adapter entry point. |
| `container.attachShadow({ mode: "open" })` | Adapter | Shadow DOM is a host-side concern. Stays in the projection adapter layer. Never crosses the worker boundary. |
| `document.createElement("style")` | Adapter | Stylesheet injection is host-side. Stays in adapter. |
| `document.createElement("div")` | Adapter | DOM construction is host-side. Stays in adapter. |
| `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate` | Adapter | Whole-page sovereignty assumption in TW5's own template. The transclude call stays inside this file and nowhere else. |
| `tw.rootWidget.domNodes = [inner]` | Adapter | TW5 internal event dispatch requires a root domNode. Stays in adapter, explicitly documented as TW5-internal plumbing. |
| `setPalette(engine, paletteName)` | Constitutional | Writes a tiddler into the wiki. No DOM dependency. An isomorphic helper. |
| `setBootSplash(engine, active)` | Constitutional | Writes/deletes a state tiddler. No DOM dependency. |

!!! packages/lararium-tw5/src/index.ts

| Export | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `mountPanel` | Adapter | Re-exported from the `tw5-browser-surface.ts` module, the one adapter version. |
| `setPalette` | Constitutional | An isomorphic helper that `@lararium/tw5` exports. |
| `setBootSplash` | Constitutional | Same as `setPalette`. |
| `mountCamera`, `CameraMount` | Constitutional | Isomorphic. No DOM dependency. Central to the projection contract. |

!!! packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-vm.ts

| Shore | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `TW5Engine.$tw` | Constitutional | The engine object itself is isomorphic. No DOM types inside. |
| `TW5Engine.fakeDocument` | Constitutional | `TW5FakeDocument` — fake DOM for TW5 filter/render work. Not a real browser document. Stays in `@lararium/tw5`. |
| `TW5Engine.rootWidget` | Constitutional | Isomorphic TW5 widget root. No `HTMLElement` dependency. |
| `mountPanel → tw5-browser-surface.ts` (comment) | Constitutional | The comment names the boundary. |

!!! packages/lararium-mesh/src/vm-pool.ts

| Shore | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `VmPool<T>` | Constitutional | Isomorphic. Already generic. The `BrowserAuthorityPool` in `@lararium/browser` extends or wraps this — does not replace it. |

!!! packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-worker-proxy.ts

| Shore | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `AnyWorker` type | Constitutional | Already platform-agnostic. Handles both Node `Worker` and browser `Web Worker` message APIs. |
| `TW5WorkerProxy` | Constitutional | Already designed for browser use. Core of the worker boot. The browser worker runtime in `@lararium/browser` uses it; `@lararium/tw5` carries the shared proxy class. |
| `WorkerFactory` type | Constitutional | Caller supplies the island constructor. Browser factory goes in `@lararium/browser`; node factory stays in `@lararium/node`. |

!!! The browser shore

`packages/lararium-browser/` carries the browser vessel: local persistence, worker lifecycle, browser
capabilities, projection return legs, and the host-side vessel composition. The page shell in
`@lararium/web` composes the visible host surface around that vessel and stays a separate layer.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/adapter-boundary`>>

!! Named Adapter Boundary

All TW5-engine DOM references that attach a rendered TW5 surface collect in one named file:
`tw5-browser-surface.ts` (in `@lararium/tw5`). This is the TW5 projection adapter boundary: it contains
the RootTemplate transclusion and TW5's real-DOM attachment compromises. The web surface may use page DOM to
compose its host surface and relay interaction; that page DOM does not become TW5 authority or a second
engine. Every entry in the Adapter class above must route through this file. No worker-side TW5 authority
may import from `window`, `document`, or `HTMLElement` without an explicit inventory entry here.

Future HUD surfaces (canvas, UE, Mudlet) bypass this file entirely — they use the island authority's projection interface directly.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/deletion-targets`>>

!! Patterns That Stay Out

These patterns stay out of the package and out of worker-side authority.

| Pattern | Why | Route instead |
|---|---|---|
| `document.createElement(...)` outside the named adapter boundary | Any occurrence outside `tw5-browser-surface.ts` marks a DOM shore that escaped the boundary | Route through the adapter or project into the worker's fakeDocument |
| `window.$tw` | Page-global authority root | Island authority via `TW5WorkerProxy` |
| Whole-page wiki boot (any code that runs TW5Engine and then attaches to `document.body` directly) | Page-singleton sovereignty | `openBrowserVessel()` → pool → worker → lease → frame |
| `tw.rootWidget.domNodes = [...]` assignment outside the adapter | Leaks DOM binding into the authority layer | Keep in the adapter only |

<<~/ahu>>

